{
  "title": "colorExpr demo \u2014 attention heatmap",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "title": "colorExpr demo \u2014 attention heatmap",
      "description": "A 6x6 row-stochastic matrix. Each cell's colour is its own `colorExpr` through the viridis ramp.",
      "markdown": "# colorExpr demo\n\nEach of the 36 cells is one `animated_polygon` with a scalar `colorExpr` mapped through `colorMap: \"viridis\"`.\n\nRow $i$ is a softmax over scores $s_{ij} = e^{-|i-j|\\cdot k}$, so every row sums to 1. Drag **sharpness** to watch the rows go from uniform to near-diagonal.",
